1
00:00:05,568 --> 00:00:06,611
A documentary?

2
00:00:06,694 --> 00:00:09,239
Do you know a show called
<i>Document Memoreal?</i>

3
00:00:09,322 --> 00:00:10,156
I know it.

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,033
It's that famous
day-in-the-life show, right?

5
00:00:12,116 --> 00:00:16,371
That show called and said
they want to do a feature on me.

6
00:00:16,454 --> 00:00:18,164
Say what?

7
00:00:18,248 --> 00:00:19,958
Maybe I'll turn it down.

8
00:00:20,041 --> 00:00:22,710
<i>Actors are supposed to keep</i>
<i>their private lives a mystery!</i>

9
00:00:22,794 --> 00:00:25,296
You can't afford
to have such picky standards!

10
00:00:26,381 --> 00:00:27,632
I guess I'll take it!

11
00:00:27,715 --> 00:00:32,095
<i>He definitely thinks he'll go viral</i>
<i>and become popular after the show.</i>

12
00:00:32,178 --> 00:00:34,639
<i>I wonder if things</i>
<i>will really go that well.</i>

13
00:00:35,223 --> 00:00:37,851
Good morning.
I'm Torihara from <i>Document Memoreal</i>.

14
00:00:37,934 --> 00:00:39,727
This is my manager.

15
00:00:39,811 --> 00:00:40,645
Konta…

16
00:00:40,728 --> 00:00:41,855
Just play along.

17
00:00:41,938 --> 00:00:44,190
I look forward to working with you all!

18
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:45,567
The pleasure is ours!

19
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:46,901
Thank you.

20
00:01:20,018 --> 00:01:21,102
I practice every day,

21
00:01:21,186 --> 00:01:24,439
so that I'm ready no matter
what kind of role comes my way.

22
00:01:24,522 --> 00:01:26,232
You are an example for all actors.

23
00:01:26,816 --> 00:01:29,444
After stage combat practice,
I go for a run.

24
00:01:30,153 --> 00:01:33,990
This is my usual routine,
so Torihara, let's go.

25
00:01:34,490 --> 00:01:37,911
He's never gone for a run even once.

26
00:01:38,661 --> 00:01:40,288
-Midori!
-What?

27
00:01:40,371 --> 00:01:43,166
Make today's BBQ extra fancy!
So it looks good on camera.

28
00:01:43,249 --> 00:01:44,125
What's that about?

29
00:01:44,208 --> 00:01:47,670
Put it on skewers to make it look nice.
Buy some good meat too. Beef please!

30
00:01:47,754 --> 00:01:50,465
Our usual meat should be fine!
I'm even making sauce for it.

31
00:01:50,548 --> 00:01:52,550
I don't want people to find out I'm poor!

32
00:01:52,634 --> 00:01:53,635
Pork also tastes good!

33
00:01:53,718 --> 00:01:57,847
-Please! Beef please!
-Are you that desperate?

34
00:01:58,473 --> 00:02:00,141
The sea feels good, right?

35
00:02:00,225 --> 00:02:01,976
-It's nice.
-Pleasant, right?

36
00:02:02,769 --> 00:02:03,895
Wait a second…

37
00:02:05,104 --> 00:02:08,983
For us actors,
our bodies are our greatest asset.

38
00:02:09,067 --> 00:02:12,195
So… I spare nothing…
when it comes to training.

39
00:02:12,278 --> 00:02:13,529
You're amazing.

40
00:02:13,613 --> 00:02:17,325
Um… Four tomatoes cost 200 yen,

41
00:02:17,408 --> 00:02:19,244
but I only want to buy one.

42
00:02:19,327 --> 00:02:20,245
Not all four?

43
00:02:20,328 --> 00:02:22,205
I only need one right now.

44
00:02:22,288 --> 00:02:24,832
I'm not great at division.

45
00:02:24,916 --> 00:02:28,127
I'm better at multiplication.
But anyway, how much for one?

46
00:02:28,211 --> 00:02:29,003
It's 50 yen.

47
00:02:29,587 --> 00:02:30,880
-Fifty?
-Yeah.

48
00:02:30,964 --> 00:02:31,965
You didn't know?

49
00:02:32,048 --> 00:02:33,216
-I did know.
-You did?

50
00:02:33,299 --> 00:02:36,261
Twenty, forty, fifty… Okay.

51
00:02:39,305 --> 00:02:41,099
Can you cut what we just said?

52
00:02:41,182 --> 00:02:42,016
Sure.

53
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:44,060
-For us actors…
-Yes.

54
00:02:44,143 --> 00:02:45,561
-Our body is our capital.
-Yes.

55
00:02:45,645 --> 00:02:47,689
So I'm careful about what I eat.

56
00:02:47,772 --> 00:02:50,358
Oh, that's great.

57
00:02:50,441 --> 00:02:51,401
Okay.

58
00:02:51,484 --> 00:02:52,652
So good.

59
00:02:54,153 --> 00:02:55,321
Huh?

60
00:02:56,239 --> 00:02:58,408
I can really taste the sun.

61
00:02:58,992 --> 00:03:01,160
-Wow, tomatoes really suit you.
-Mr. Nishigami!

62
00:03:15,383 --> 00:03:21,681
Mr. Konta. I was just about
to come over and deliver some fish.

63
00:03:21,764 --> 00:03:23,391
Yay, awesome!

64
00:03:23,474 --> 00:03:26,394
Mr. Nishigami, today's barbecue
is super fancy, so why don't you join us?

65
00:03:27,228 --> 00:03:28,771
-May I?
-Of course.

66
00:03:29,355 --> 00:03:31,566
-Mr. Konta. Who is this man?
-Huh?

67
00:03:31,649 --> 00:03:34,235
-Huh? Are you curious about him?
-Yes.

68
00:03:34,318 --> 00:03:35,486
Well…

69
00:03:36,279 --> 00:03:39,657
This is Mr. Nishigami.
He manages this entire area.

70
00:03:41,617 --> 00:03:42,827
Wow.

71
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:44,412
What a handsome man.

72
00:03:46,456 --> 00:03:47,999
Mr. Torihara.

73
00:03:48,082 --> 00:03:51,252
Please don't film that man.
He's just a regular person.

74
00:03:51,336 --> 00:03:54,964
He's regular people.
Please film me. I'm the professional here.

75
00:03:55,048 --> 00:03:57,633
He's just an ordinary guy,
totally ordinary.

76
00:03:57,717 --> 00:04:00,428
It's just that he's quite tall,
has a small face,

77
00:04:00,511 --> 00:04:01,637
and he's cool too!

78
00:04:02,305 --> 00:04:04,182
Who's that, Chainsaw Woman?

79
00:04:04,265 --> 00:04:05,892
Please film me!

80
00:04:07,018 --> 00:04:09,020
-What was that noise?
-Sorry.

81
00:04:10,730 --> 00:04:13,066
Our food looks fancy today.

82
00:04:13,149 --> 00:04:15,234
I'm just putting them on skewers, though.

83
00:04:15,318 --> 00:04:17,236
But I actually bought beef.

84
00:04:17,945 --> 00:04:19,947
We need to save money later.

85
00:04:20,031 --> 00:04:24,327
It would be great
if this really makes Konta successful.

86
00:04:25,453 --> 00:04:27,038
I'm worried.

87
00:04:27,121 --> 00:04:29,332
It's like my brother
has completely changed

88
00:04:29,415 --> 00:04:31,376
since the show started.

89
00:04:32,877 --> 00:04:34,003
No! The meat!

90
00:04:34,087 --> 00:04:36,756
-Oh, crap…
-It's fine. I'll do it. Give.

91
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:45,807
He doesn't need to put on a show.
I prefer him as he is.

92
00:04:48,226 --> 00:04:50,436
You like him as he is?

93
00:05:04,575 --> 00:05:08,079
Mr. Nishigami!

94
00:05:08,996 --> 00:05:10,373
I'm doing an interview now.

95
00:05:10,957 --> 00:05:13,292
-An interview.
-But this needs doing.

96
00:05:13,376 --> 00:05:16,504
But, I'm doing an interview.
Please quiet down a bit.

97
00:05:16,587 --> 00:05:18,089
Please! Just a little bit.

98
00:05:18,172 --> 00:05:19,757
One more time.

99
00:05:19,841 --> 00:05:21,092
Once more?

100
00:05:22,343 --> 00:05:24,804
You look great. Like a magazine cover.

101
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:28,474
A magazine cover, huh?
I would love to do one.

102
00:05:28,558 --> 00:05:31,269
"I'll buy it because Konta Hoshino
is on the cover."

103
00:05:31,352 --> 00:05:33,688
"I'll watch it
because Konta Hoshino is in it."

104
00:05:33,771 --> 00:05:38,067
I want to create
a Konta Hoshino sensation like that.

105
00:05:38,693 --> 00:05:40,027
That's nice.

106
00:05:40,111 --> 00:05:42,488
<i>Hey, Mr. Nishigami!</i>

107
00:05:42,572 --> 00:05:45,199
<i>Hey, are you filming me?</i>

108
00:05:45,283 --> 00:05:47,118
-Are you?
-That was a group shot.

109
00:05:47,201 --> 00:05:48,578
Please do it right.

110
00:05:52,748 --> 00:05:53,749
Excuse me.

111
00:05:54,375 --> 00:05:55,543
<i>It's a call from…</i>

112
00:05:56,377 --> 00:05:58,421
<i>the actor Jin Ichijo.</i>

113
00:05:59,297 --> 00:06:01,090
<i>-May I take it?</i>
<i>-Go ahead.</i>

114
00:06:03,217 --> 00:06:05,720
<i>Hello, Mr. Jin? Yeah, what's up?</i>

115
00:06:06,387 --> 00:06:08,472
<i>Oh, the other day.</i>

116
00:06:08,556 --> 00:06:10,766
<i>No, thank you! Yeah.</i>

117
00:06:10,850 --> 00:06:15,771
<i>Come hang out any time.</i>
<i>All right, have a nice summer vacation!</i>

118
00:06:17,190 --> 00:06:19,942
Wait, do you know Jin Ichijo?

119
00:06:20,026 --> 00:06:21,527
We are acquaintances.

120
00:06:22,111 --> 00:06:23,487
-I've acted with him too.
-What?

121
00:06:23,571 --> 00:06:25,448
-We're basically bros.
-Wow!

122
00:06:25,531 --> 00:06:29,869
We have a great
give-and-take relationship.

123
00:06:29,952 --> 00:06:32,330
That's amazing.

124
00:06:34,081 --> 00:06:34,999
Excuse me…

125
00:06:35,082 --> 00:06:36,250
Yes?

126
00:06:36,334 --> 00:06:39,295
-Just a moment. Hold on.
-What's wrong?

127
00:06:40,379 --> 00:06:42,173
Hello, Mr. Jin?

128
00:06:42,256 --> 00:06:45,051
No, that's not it. I'm sorry.

129
00:06:45,134 --> 00:06:48,346
I'm filming for a show
called <i>Document Memoreal</i>.

130
00:06:48,429 --> 00:06:52,391
Yes, exactly. So, I guess
I got too excited.

131
00:06:52,934 --> 00:06:54,560
Sorry. I'm sorry.

132
00:06:55,228 --> 00:06:56,896
Thank you very much. I'll do my best.

133
00:06:56,979 --> 00:07:00,358
By the way, Mr. Jin,
give me some work once in a while.

134
00:07:00,441 --> 00:07:03,361
No matter how small the role…
Even a tiny role. I'll do it.

135
00:07:03,444 --> 00:07:06,989
Yes, please. Goodbye.

136
00:07:09,742 --> 00:07:12,620
-Hey, stop the camera!
-Sorry.

137
00:07:12,703 --> 00:07:14,121
By the way, what was that?

138
00:07:14,205 --> 00:07:15,289
What?

139
00:07:15,373 --> 00:07:17,250
Just utilities.

140
00:07:17,333 --> 00:07:18,709
-Utilities?
-They called me…

141
00:07:18,793 --> 00:07:20,378
Konta, let's start the barbecue.

142
00:07:20,461 --> 00:07:21,671
Okay!

143
00:07:21,754 --> 00:07:23,839
Oh, I'll make a drink for you.

144
00:07:23,923 --> 00:07:24,757
You will?

145
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:27,593
-But cut out that part earlier.
-Okay.

146
00:07:27,677 --> 00:07:32,056
Konta Hoshino doesn't
squeeze it like this, but like this!

147
00:07:32,139 --> 00:07:34,308
-Oh, nice. How dynamic.
-Like this!

148
00:07:34,392 --> 00:07:36,394
Then with my other hand…

149
00:07:36,477 --> 00:07:38,813
-Like this!
-Oh, very nice.

150
00:07:39,564 --> 00:07:41,107
Mr. Manager.

151
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:42,275
Mr. Manager.

152
00:07:42,358 --> 00:07:44,443
Yes? Oh, me?

153
00:07:44,527 --> 00:07:47,572
If you have any footage
of his past works or audition tapes,

154
00:07:47,655 --> 00:07:49,615
could we borrow them to use as material?

155
00:07:50,449 --> 00:07:52,076
Materials, got it.

156
00:07:52,159 --> 00:07:53,119
Thanks.

157
00:07:53,202 --> 00:07:55,162
Mr. Torihara. I'll make you a drink.

158
00:07:55,246 --> 00:07:57,206
But I'm still on the clock.

159
00:07:57,290 --> 00:07:58,332
It's totally fine.

160
00:07:58,416 --> 00:08:01,419
However, if you drink this,
you'll turn stupid!

161
00:08:01,502 --> 00:08:02,295
What?

162
00:08:02,378 --> 00:08:06,549
Okay, it's time for
Konta Hoshino's half-assed cooking!

163
00:08:07,758 --> 00:08:11,387
So, you know the familiar
lemon sour mix and gum syrup.

164
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:14,140
Normally, you put them in one by one,
but I'm an expert.

165
00:08:14,223 --> 00:08:18,436
I'll just pour them in at the same time.
Pouring them in. I'll just eyeball it.

166
00:08:18,519 --> 00:08:19,895
I'm even closing my eyes.

167
00:08:19,979 --> 00:08:23,482
-Konta, stop!
-This much should be about right. More!

168
00:08:23,566 --> 00:08:27,069
I'll squint and check.
This should be enough, right?

169
00:08:27,153 --> 00:08:29,614
-Next, pour in the soda.
-Yes.

170
00:08:29,697 --> 00:08:33,200
Fizz… I'm also eyeballing it
while closing my eyes.

171
00:08:33,284 --> 00:08:34,285
You close your eyes?

172
00:08:34,368 --> 00:08:36,037
Is this about right?

173
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,830
-Konta!
-Just in time!

174
00:08:37,913 --> 00:08:42,251
Here you go, Mr. Torihara.
It's done. Drink up!

175
00:08:42,335 --> 00:08:43,878
Oh, thank you.

176
00:08:43,961 --> 00:08:45,171
Go ahead.

177
00:08:49,383 --> 00:08:50,593
It has a stupid taste.

178
00:08:50,676 --> 00:08:52,762
Yeah, exactly. It makes you stupid.

179
00:08:56,641 --> 00:08:58,976
Midori, you're awesome!

180
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:00,144
You bought beef.

181
00:09:00,227 --> 00:09:01,771
Yeah, I did.

182
00:09:01,854 --> 00:09:06,400
This is <i>acqua pazza</i> made with
the sea bream Mr. Nishigami brought us!

183
00:09:06,484 --> 00:09:07,943
What's <i>acqua pazza</i>?

184
00:09:08,027 --> 00:09:09,904
-It's <i>acqua pazza</i>.
-What is "<i>pazza</i>"?

185
00:09:09,987 --> 00:09:11,072
What?

186
00:09:11,155 --> 00:09:13,366
What's with your reaction?

187
00:09:13,449 --> 00:09:15,785
Did you make this, Ms. Midori?

188
00:09:15,868 --> 00:09:19,163
Yes. It's full of nature's blessings.

189
00:09:21,707 --> 00:09:23,167
It's beautiful.

190
00:09:24,835 --> 00:09:26,170
Let's eat, okay?

191
00:09:26,253 --> 00:09:28,172
-Looks delicious, for sure.
-Go ahead.

192
00:09:28,255 --> 00:09:30,549
-It looks great.
-Slide it out…

193
00:09:32,468 --> 00:09:33,844
Done!

194
00:09:33,928 --> 00:09:35,137
Here, Mr. Nishigami.

195
00:09:35,221 --> 00:09:36,847
Thank you very much.

196
00:09:36,931 --> 00:09:41,143
My little sister is a genius at cooking.
Everything she makes tastes amazing!

197
00:09:41,227 --> 00:09:42,436
That's impressive.

198
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,730
Mr. Torihara, you don't need
to keep filming. Let's eat.

199
00:09:44,814 --> 00:09:46,357
-What?
-I'll serve some for you, here.

200
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:47,525
All right.

201
00:09:47,608 --> 00:09:49,985
Wait, Konta, that's too much.

202
00:09:50,069 --> 00:09:52,988
Mr. Torihara has been filming me
all day today.

203
00:09:53,072 --> 00:09:56,367
His stomach must be rumbling,
so he needs to eat at least this much.

204
00:09:56,450 --> 00:09:58,869
-Thank you very much.
-Come on, give me the camera.

205
00:09:58,953 --> 00:10:00,413
Maybe I'll film.

206
00:10:01,414 --> 00:10:04,875
-It's all just salad.
-A gathering of amateurs!

207
00:10:04,959 --> 00:10:07,878
A gathering of amateurs!
We're all amateurs, all right.

208
00:10:07,962 --> 00:10:08,796
That's true.

209
00:10:10,089 --> 00:10:13,467
Mr. Konta, have you ever
held a regular job?

210
00:10:13,551 --> 00:10:15,010
A job, huh…

211
00:10:15,845 --> 00:10:18,556
Acting is my true calling.

212
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:22,476
I will be an actor forever.

213
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,478
Then what about part-time jobs?

214
00:10:25,187 --> 00:10:26,522
Right, yes.

215
00:10:27,148 --> 00:10:29,817
I've done various part-time jobs.

216
00:10:30,901 --> 00:10:34,905
But I believe all of it
feeds into my acting.

217
00:10:36,991 --> 00:10:38,576
By the way, what about now?

218
00:10:39,744 --> 00:10:41,996
Oh, I focus solely on acting.

219
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:47,251
I only do part-time jobs occasionally,
for role research.

220
00:10:49,003 --> 00:10:53,132
Why did you decide to become an actor?

221
00:10:59,054 --> 00:11:04,894
When I was in the third grade,
I acted in <i>Momotaro </i>for a school play.

222
00:11:05,853 --> 00:11:09,064
At that time, it was so much fun.

223
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:12,485
I just had a very minor role, though.

224
00:11:14,111 --> 00:11:16,906
Being able to become someone
other than myself

225
00:11:17,573 --> 00:11:21,577
to me, was a very happy moment.

226
00:11:22,745 --> 00:11:27,041
I think, I was born to act.

227
00:11:27,124 --> 00:11:30,211
I was born for that purpose.
I truly believe that.

228
00:11:30,961 --> 00:11:34,131
Midori also supports me.

229
00:11:35,925 --> 00:11:39,053
Everyone is supporting me,
so I want to get on top,

230
00:11:40,596 --> 00:11:42,056
for their sake.

231
00:11:52,107 --> 00:11:55,694
Torihara, I saw the footage you got.

232
00:11:55,778 --> 00:11:59,448
It's good. But if we inflate his ego more,
we can film something way funnier.

233
00:11:59,532 --> 00:12:02,034
Yes, but about that…

234
00:12:02,117 --> 00:12:07,164
Let him run amok,
and give us lots of smug faces.

235
00:12:08,582 --> 00:12:12,711
It's better to exaggerate things.
That's what the viewers are looking for.

236
00:12:15,214 --> 00:12:16,048
Yes.

237
00:12:16,799 --> 00:12:17,925
I understand.

238
00:12:29,937 --> 00:12:31,105
Good morning.

239
00:12:31,188 --> 00:12:32,356
Oh, good morning.

240
00:12:32,439 --> 00:12:33,899
Where is Mr. Konta?

241
00:12:33,983 --> 00:12:35,693
He left a little while ago.

242
00:12:35,776 --> 00:12:38,112
Lately, he has been going out
a lot in the morning.

243
00:12:38,195 --> 00:12:39,822
But I think he'll be back soon.

244
00:12:39,905 --> 00:12:41,490
It's so early. Where did he go?

245
00:12:42,116 --> 00:12:45,578
It seems he's helping out the neighbors.

246
00:12:45,661 --> 00:12:46,829
Helping out?

247
00:12:46,912 --> 00:12:49,665
Oh! But I don't think
he wants that part to be filmed.

248
00:12:49,748 --> 00:12:50,958
But I've got to film that!

249
00:12:51,041 --> 00:12:53,544
Huh? No, maybe you shouldn't?

250
00:12:53,627 --> 00:12:55,045
I'll just go check it out.

251
00:12:55,129 --> 00:12:57,423
-Huh? Wait…
-I'm off!

252
00:12:58,882 --> 00:12:59,883
Oh, boy.

253
00:13:02,511 --> 00:13:03,762
Well, not my problem.

254
00:13:05,055 --> 00:13:07,850
Good morning, ma'am!

255
00:13:07,933 --> 00:13:09,810
All right, shall we get to it?

256
00:13:09,893 --> 00:13:11,395
Sorry for making you do this.

257
00:13:11,478 --> 00:13:13,689
Don't be. You look beautiful today too.

258
00:13:13,772 --> 00:13:14,690
Thank you.

259
00:13:14,773 --> 00:13:15,733
All right!

260
00:13:17,901 --> 00:13:19,236
-Konta.
-Yes!

261
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,447
I have some tea here.
Make sure to drink it.

262
00:13:21,530 --> 00:13:25,159
Oh, thank you. Hup.

263
00:13:25,242 --> 00:13:27,036
Hup!

264
00:13:27,119 --> 00:13:30,664
Wait! That isn't a weed. Don't pull it.

265
00:13:30,748 --> 00:13:32,499
Huh? This isn't a weed?

266
00:13:32,583 --> 00:13:34,418
It's mugwort I'm carefully growing.

267
00:13:34,501 --> 00:13:36,503
Oh, ma'am, I'm sorry.

268
00:13:36,587 --> 00:13:38,255
My goodness Konta…

269
00:13:38,339 --> 00:13:39,465
Wait, can you eat this?

270
00:13:39,548 --> 00:13:40,716
Yes, you can.

271
00:13:43,552 --> 00:13:46,847
Oh, you're right.
It tastes like mugwort mochi.

272
00:13:47,556 --> 00:13:48,557
Wow, it's good.

273
00:13:49,350 --> 00:13:50,184
I can't stop.

274
00:13:50,768 --> 00:13:51,685
It's good.

275
00:13:52,311 --> 00:13:53,395
It's actually good!

276
00:13:53,479 --> 00:13:55,230
Come on, don't eat so much.

277
00:13:55,314 --> 00:13:56,231
Do you want some?

278
00:13:56,315 --> 00:13:57,232
What?

279
00:13:57,316 --> 00:13:59,735
Please make some mugwort mochi with this.

280
00:13:59,818 --> 00:14:00,861
-What? With this?
-Yes.

281
00:14:00,944 --> 00:14:04,323
Mugwort mochi is just mugwort
and rice cake, so you can make it, right?

282
00:14:04,406 --> 00:14:05,324
It's not that simple.

283
00:14:05,407 --> 00:14:06,784
Oh, I see.

284
00:14:08,827 --> 00:14:10,287
-Konta.
-Yes?

285
00:14:10,371 --> 00:14:12,247
Thanks for your hard work. Have this.

286
00:14:13,374 --> 00:14:14,375
Huh?

287
00:14:15,793 --> 00:14:17,461
Thank you!

288
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:21,382
Mrs. Kawamoto next door
wants to ask you to walk Pero.

289
00:14:21,465 --> 00:14:24,760
-Okay. See you later.
-Get on it, okay?

290
00:14:24,843 --> 00:14:26,929
Once I become successful,
I'll repay you all!

291
00:14:27,012 --> 00:14:28,055
-Sure.
-Bye now.

292
00:14:28,138 --> 00:14:29,723
-Bye, see you later!
-Bye!

293
00:14:29,807 --> 00:14:32,977
Wait, Pero!

294
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:35,688
Hold on, Pero!

295
00:14:35,771 --> 00:14:40,401
Pero! Wait! Pero!

296
00:14:40,484 --> 00:14:42,403
Pero!

297
00:14:49,368 --> 00:14:54,498
Heave-ho!

298
00:14:55,916 --> 00:14:58,711
Heave-ho!

299
00:14:59,837 --> 00:15:02,589
Oh! Heave-ho!

300
00:15:08,804 --> 00:15:09,638
Thank you.

301
00:15:09,722 --> 00:15:11,306
No, thank you as well.

302
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:13,142
-Mister, your hat is nice.
-Thank you.

303
00:15:13,225 --> 00:15:15,728
-Can I have it?
-Huh? Give it back!

304
00:15:15,811 --> 00:15:18,272
Hey! Give it to me!

305
00:15:20,232 --> 00:15:22,568
Nice! Okay.

306
00:15:28,824 --> 00:15:30,117
What?

307
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:34,705
All right! One, two, three bills…

308
00:15:35,247 --> 00:15:36,915
That's 15,000 yen!

309
00:15:36,999 --> 00:15:38,042
Mr. Konta!

310
00:15:38,125 --> 00:15:40,252
Mr. Torihara, hello.

311
00:15:40,335 --> 00:15:42,713
-Looking forward to filming today!
-No.

312
00:15:42,796 --> 00:15:46,341
-Actually, Konta, I'm heading back now.
-Huh? What?

313
00:15:46,425 --> 00:15:48,969
I have already sufficiently
captured your charm.

314
00:15:49,678 --> 00:15:52,556
But it has only been yesterday.
Aren't you going to film today too?

315
00:15:52,639 --> 00:15:55,017
I understand your good qualities
very well now.

316
00:15:55,768 --> 00:15:57,519
-Oh, is that so?
-Yes.

317
00:15:57,603 --> 00:15:59,104
Look forward to the broadcast.

318
00:15:59,188 --> 00:16:00,022
I will.

319
00:16:00,105 --> 00:16:01,440
Well, excuse me.

320
00:16:02,024 --> 00:16:04,109
-Wait, you understand my good qualities?
-Yes!

321
00:16:04,193 --> 00:16:06,737
Okay. Wait, what are they?

322
00:16:06,820 --> 00:16:07,905
Watch it when it airs!

323
00:16:07,988 --> 00:16:10,115
No, I want to know my good qualities!

324
00:16:10,199 --> 00:16:11,867
-I can't tell you.
-I don't know…

325
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:13,660
No? Why can't you tell me?

326
00:16:13,744 --> 00:16:16,330
-Please watch it on air.
-Does that mean I don't have any?

327
00:16:16,413 --> 00:16:18,123
No, just watch the show!

328
00:16:25,422 --> 00:16:29,009
Document Memoreal<i>. I watch it too.</i>

329
00:16:29,968 --> 00:16:30,886
I see.

330
00:16:32,221 --> 00:16:34,765
You watch it too, Lady Yomi?

331
00:16:35,724 --> 00:16:40,187
<i>I like their large family special,</i>
<i>"We are! The 1,000-Person Family."</i>

332
00:16:41,188 --> 00:16:45,567
<i>But it's ironic.</i>
<i>Just when he's finally getting on TV,</i>

333
00:16:45,651 --> 00:16:47,986
<i>he doesn't have long to live.</i>

334
00:16:48,070 --> 00:16:51,865
<i>Well, if he hasn't</i>
<i>become famous by that age,</i>

335
00:16:51,949 --> 00:16:54,326
<i>he isn't going to become a star now.</i>

336
00:16:54,409 --> 00:16:58,413
<i>All that's left is to quietly wait</i>
<i>for death at the end of summer.</i>

337
00:16:59,623 --> 00:17:01,625
I think so too, but…

338
00:17:08,882 --> 00:17:11,093
They pursue their dreams, have hope…

339
00:17:12,052 --> 00:17:15,472
and try to live out their days
the best they can.

340
00:17:17,808 --> 00:17:18,892
That's what

341
00:17:19,893 --> 00:17:21,728
makes them human, I think.

342
00:17:23,856 --> 00:17:25,190
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

343
00:17:25,983 --> 00:17:28,569
<i>You sound like a human.</i>
<i>Don't say things like that.</i>

344
00:17:30,654 --> 00:17:31,655
My apologies.

345
00:17:34,408 --> 00:17:38,412
<i>It is forbidden for a Grim Reaper</i>
<i>to feel affection for humans.</i>

346
00:17:38,495 --> 00:17:42,082
<i>The fates of Grim Reapers</i>
<i>and humans do not cross.</i>

347
00:17:42,166 --> 00:17:46,795
<i>You must devote yourself entirely</i>
<i>to witnessing their lifespans.</i>

348
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:49,423
Understood.

349
00:17:51,884 --> 00:17:52,885
That is…

350
00:17:55,721 --> 00:17:57,431
my mission, after all.

351
00:18:19,411 --> 00:18:21,955
<i>-Midori, it's starting, hurry!</i>
<i>-Wait for me!</i>

352
00:18:22,581 --> 00:18:24,166
-There it is.
-It's started!

353
00:18:24,249 --> 00:18:25,125
It's started.

354
00:18:25,209 --> 00:18:26,668
I am…

355
00:18:26,752 --> 00:18:28,003
Konta Hoshino.

356
00:18:28,086 --> 00:18:29,379
Then please get Koji Yakusho.

357
00:18:29,463 --> 00:18:30,547
One more time!

358
00:18:30,631 --> 00:18:33,425
If they edit it like that,
it will make me look bad.

359
00:18:33,508 --> 00:18:36,345
<i>The editing is just malicious, isn't it?</i>

360
00:18:36,428 --> 00:18:38,222
<i>We are unemployed, living on benefits…</i>

361
00:18:38,305 --> 00:18:39,514
Jobless?

362
00:18:39,598 --> 00:18:41,099
I'm being made a fool of!

363
00:18:41,183 --> 00:18:42,935
Even a tiny role. I'll do it!

364
00:18:43,018 --> 00:18:44,853
What is this? Did he secretly film me?

365
00:18:44,937 --> 00:18:47,981
<i>The heck? Mr. Torihara betrayed me.</i>

366
00:18:48,065 --> 00:18:51,276
I think this episode
turned out quite well.

367
00:18:52,361 --> 00:18:54,404
<i>My acting career is over.</i>

368
00:18:54,488 --> 00:18:55,447
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

